╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hierarchical_adaptive_encoder                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This approach replaces the linear chain ansatz with a hierarchical adaptive encoding      │
│                          │ strategy that:                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Shared parameters across uploads**: Instead of N_UPLOADS * N_REPEATS unique          │
│                          │ parameter sets, we reuse the same ~20 parameters across all blocks. This acts as implicit │
│                          │ regularization, forcing the circuit to learn generalizable transformations rather than    │
│                          │ memorizing training data.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Data-adaptive gates**: Replace all single-qubit rotations with CRX/CRY gates         │
│                          │ controlled by feature information encoded in other qubits. This allows the circuit to     │
│                          │ dynamically adjust based on input features, improving feature extraction while keeping    │
│                          │ parameter count low.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **All-to-all entangling pattern**: Replace the linear CZ chain with a star topology    │
│                          │ (hub qubit entangles with all others), then alternate with different hubs. This provides  │
│                          │ richer connectivity for 8 qubits without excessive depth, allowing features on any pair   │
│                          │ to interact directly.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Shallow per-block design**: Reduce from 23 gates per block to ~16 gates (3 adaptive  │
│                          │ layers + 7 entangling gates), cutting circuit depth by ~30% while maintaining             │
│                          │ expressivity through careful gate selection.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Symmetry breaking**: Use distinct parameter names strategically to break symmetries  │
│                          │ while still maintaining parameter sharing across uploads.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected benefits:                                                                        │
│                          │ - Reduced generalization gap (fewer parameters to overfit with)                           │
│                          │ - Lower circuit depth → less noise accumulation                                           │
│                          │ - Faster convergence (fewer parameters to optimize)                                       │
│                          │ - Better parameter efficiency (adaptive gates respond to data)                            │
│                          │ - Higher test accuracy through implicit regularization                                    │
