│                          │ qubit pairs                                                                               │
│                          │ 2. **Program 2** (score 0.87): 122 params, more complex with 8 distinct CRY keys in first │
│                          │ layer and 4 in second layer                                                               │
│                          │ 3. **Current** (score 0.86): 92 params, uses CRZ gates with moderate parameter sharing    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Program 2 achieved the highest score (0.87) despite having more parameters, suggesting  │
│                          │ that **strategic parameter sharing across entangling layers** improves generalization     │
│                          │ - The current program has a generalization gap of 0.08 (train 0.95, test 0.87),           │
│                          │ indicating overfitting                                                                    │
│                          │ - Program 2 had lower generalization gap (0.04) with better validation accuracy (0.90)    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **New strategy**: Implement aggressive parameter sharing by:                              │
│                          │ 1. Using CRY gates (which performed well in Program 2) instead of CRZ                     │
│                          │ 2. **Sharing CRY parameters across both entangling sublayers** (first layer uses cry_01,  │
│                          │ cry_23, cry_45, cry_67; second layer reuses the same keys for cry_12, cry_34, cry_56,     │
│                          │ cry_70)                                                                                   │
│                          │ 3. Reducing total parameters while maintaining expressiveness through strategic           │
│                          │ connectivity                                                                              │
│                          │ 4. Keeping RY/RZ sharing to reduce single-qubit parameter count                           │
│                          │ 5. This reduces N_params_per_block from current ~11 to ~8, cutting total params to ~50    │
│                          │ while preserving the two-qubit interaction patterns that worked well                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
